{"absent":["Full layout of the s5 view whose head lies outside the routed tail.","Register access effects, clear behavior, ordering, locking and concurrency rules for the event status words.","Consumers, handlers, entry points, exports and acknowledgement or state machine behavior for these events.","Mask for the third graphics group one translation event and all later group one definitions beyond the truncation.","Definition and meaning of UVYH word one bits above thirty-seven and any reserved requirements there.","Reset values, reserved bit write policies and error recovery sequences."],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u"],"text":"Event status word zero is presented as one 64-bit container with distinct per-generation layouts. The routed window shows the tail of an s5 view plus complete s4, s3 and s2 views, with s4 documented for UV4 hardware and s3 and s2 for UV3 and UV2. Each complete view packs single-bit flags for block errors, shutdown, interrupts and bridge control plus reserved padding to fill the full width."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u"],"text":"The UV4 view groups early bits for per-block hard errors and two repeated banks of per-block always-on errors across fabric, transfer, routing, link, graphics, crossbar, queue and network blocks, then shutdown, sixteen local bus interrupts, nonmaskable interrupt, clock stop, bidirectional bridge signals and logic analyzer trigger, closing with interprocessor and four external input interrupts and no trailing reserved field."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u"],"text":"The UV3 and UV2 views use identical categories in this word: per-block hard errors, two banks of always-on errors, shutdown, sixteen local bus interrupts, nonmaskable interrupt, clock stop, bidirectional bridge signals, logic analyzer trigger, interprocessor interrupt, four external input interrupts, one profiling interrupt and a five-bit reserved tail. They track a queue processor block where UV4 tracks a transfer block and one routing pair where UV4 tracks four queue groups."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED0_ALIAS","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED1"],"text":"The alias for event status word zero resides at offset 0x70008 and event status word one resides at offset 0x70080."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_IPI_INT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_IPI_INT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT0_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT0_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT1_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT1_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT2_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT2_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT3_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_EXTIO_INT3_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROFILE_INT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROFILE_INT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_BAU_DATA_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_BAU_DATA_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROC_GENERAL_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROC_GENERAL_MASK"],"text":"In the UVYH layout of word one the lowest eight bit positions each carry one system event in ascending order: interprocessor notification first, then four external input events, then profiling, broadcast assist data and general processor events, each described by a shift and a matching one-bit mask."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT0_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT0_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT1_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT1_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT2_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT2_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT3_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT3_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT4_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT4_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT5_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_XH_TLB_INT5_MASK"],"text":"Continuing the same UVYH word, six cache coherence events for one translation block occupy the next six consecutive bit positions after the low system byte, each with its own shift and one-bit mask pair in numeric order."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT0_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT0_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT1_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT1_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT2_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT2_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT3_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT3_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT4_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_RDM_TLB_INT4_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.