econd event of the second group and shows only the shift of the third event."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_IPI_INT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_IPI_INT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROFILE_INT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROFILE_INT_MASK"],"text":"Every status flag in the routed views is a one-bit readable writable field, every shift and mask pair selects exactly one bit with the mask equal to one shifted by the stated shift, and reserved fields only pad the register to its full width and signal no event."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_IPI_INT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROFILE_INT_SHFT"],"text":"Identical bit offsets in word zero mean different blocks on different generations, and word one uses incompatible family layouts, so decoding with the wrong generation or family view misattributes errors and interrupts."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":74,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"90fbc6904033e42000ae762f7e22713ee62f438dcdedfc4bd7328bc76c81714c","prompt_sha256":"f5484de66b791623b7ec6bce2c193363361584ce2d9bf904b84e5db8aaeb0123","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_event_occurred0_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED0_ALIAS","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_EVENT_OCCURRED1","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_EVENT_OCCURRED1_IPI_INT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_EVENT_OCCURRED1_PROFILE_INT_SHFT"]}
